From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:04:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a compilable test map with an hgrunt for Hybrid AI Core
 testing

scripts/build-test-map.sh compiles mapsrc/*.map with the local VHLT
toolchain (hlcsg -nowadtextures, hlbsp, hlvis -fast, hlrad -bounce 2)
and deploys the .bsp straight into the test mod's maps/ folder.

mapsrc/ai_test_grunt.map (generated by mapsrc/gen_ai_test_grunt.py) is
a minimal room with a monster_human_grunt, so `ai_hybrid_debug 1`
output can be checked with `map ai_test_grunt` instead of loading a
full campaign map.

Notable pitfall hit and documented: GoldSrc/VHLT .map brush planes
need an INWARD-pointing normal, not outward as intuition suggests -
confirmed by cross-referencing a decompiled retail map. Getting it
backwards produces "Entity N, Brush M: outside world" on some faces
while others compile fine, which is hard to debug from the error text
alone. The generator computes and verifies each face's normal
programmatically instead of hand-deriving point order, and
scripts/README.md documents the gotcha for future hand-written maps.

